7" :question/id #uuid "7b31894d-8a98-5cb2-800f-c6e12082fad0" :question/math-academy-id "q-70357" :question/is-example false :question/problem "$\\frac{1}{z}+\\frac{3}{z-3}=$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we need to put the fractions over a common denominator of $z(z-3),$ since there are no common factors in either denominator that we can exploit.\n\nTo do this, we multiply the top and bottom of the first fraction by $z-3$, and the top and bottom of the second fraction by $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{z}+\\frac{3}{z-3} & = \\\\ \\frac{z-3}{z-3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{z}+\\frac{z}{z}\\cdot \\frac{3}{z-3} & = \\\\ \\frac{z-3}{z(z-3)}+\\frac{3z}{z(z-3)} & = \\\\ \\frac{z-3+3z}{z(z-3)} & = \\\\ \\frac{4z-3}{z(z-3)} & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-70357/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3db20b82-9561-5c54-8e12-8914bb6747c3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-70357"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-70359/selection/2028aa7a3d918ec7af7af95bb70f55776ef69d09a8d828c5de69f16fa3f1c889" :answer/id #uuid "401d2718-887e-554b-8971-8d418fd98913" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2x-3}{x(2x-1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70359/selection/b657d8a584a7620a6acf28805b86c0a8d478f7e9d4d9d08fec7c94e3d5116034" :answer/id #uuid "755a0bb5-46da-5d71-9713-4b80a1a22c19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2x+3}{2x-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70359/selection/24f6680785850bcdd354435e6acddde1a318298dc3db98afdea2ea25e40d9078" :answer/id #uuid "47c36c84-8d28-5f3e-a8b5-3b46722145e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2x-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70359/selection/d6fd6eb896d985f6b6185cc22ee0f4191fb807dd910737e7a1870525a8712cc2" :answer/id #uuid "0127dede-9d83-58c2-b5c8-4f0df8f08afc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{x(2x-1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70359/selection/b7af7ff53d2b1edebb71ba4af15b1a1bdf2ef61d78602adc1c2e9efd5f93d59e" :answer/id #uuid "a60e8bb7-568a-5e71-a040-f605250d504c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+6}{x(2x-1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70359/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "07dc012d-a667-5954-91d9-7aa4361493e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-70359/selection/d6fd6eb896d985f6b6185cc22ee0f4191fb807dd910737e7a1870525a8712cc2" :answer-field/choices ["q-70359/selection/2028aa7a3d918ec7af7af95bb70f55776ef69d09a8d828c5de69f16fa3f1c889" "q-70359/selection/b657d8a584a7620a6acf28805b86c0a8d478f7e9d4d9d08fec7c94e3d5116034" "q-70359/selection/24f6680785850bcdd354435e6acddde1a318298dc3db98afdea2ea25e40d9078" "q-70359/selection/d6fd6eb896d985f6b6185cc22ee0f4191fb807dd910737e7a1870525a8712cc2" "q-70359/selection/b7af7ff53d2b1edebb71ba4af15b1a1bdf2ef61d78602adc1c2e9efd5f93d59e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-70359" :question/id #uuid "4a571faa-9b3c-5aee-961d-64e751de7349" :question/math-academy-id "q-70359" :question/is-example false :question/problem "$\\frac{6}{2x-1}-\\frac{3}{x}=$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we need to put the fractions over a common denominator of $x(2x-1),$ since there are no common factors in either denominator that we can exploit. \n\nTo do this, we multiply the top and bottom of the first fraction by $x,$ and the top and bottom of the second fraction by $2x-1:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6}{2x-1}-\\frac{3}{x} & = \\\\ \\frac{x}{x}\\cdot \\frac{6}{2x-1}-\\frac{2x-1}{2x-1}\\cdot \\frac{3}{x} & = \\\\ \\frac{6x}{x(2x-1)}-\\frac{3(2x-1)}{x(2x-1)} & = \\\\ \\frac{6x-3(2x-1)}{x(2x-1)} & = \\\\ \\frac{6x-6x+3}{x(2x-1)} & = \\\\ \\frac{3}{x(2x-1)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-70359/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-poi